          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-why-infinite",
        "moduleId": "why-induction",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "为什么需要一种新证明方法",
        "markdown": "若命题对 $n=1,2,\\dots$ 都要成立，逐个代入只能覆盖有限多个 $n$，不构成对无穷多个正整数的证明。归纳法的关键转念是：不直接证明每一项，而是证明“真值可以从一项传播到下一项”，再给出传播的起点。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-problem"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-well-ordering",
        "moduleId": "why-induction",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "教材：良序原理",
        "markdown": "**良序原理（well-ordering principle）**：把一些正整数收集成非空集合，该集合中一定存在最小元素。教材在此直接把它当作公设使用，因为结论与直觉相符：正整数从 $1$ 起有下界，所以非空正整数集合不会无限向下延伸。集合可能有无限多个元素，我们未必能实际找出这个最小元素，但相信它存在。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000009"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Methods of Proof",
                "Mathematical Induction"
              ],
              "lineStart": 239,
              "lineEnd": 294,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "81684586e40aed2064248f3318f4b7188c78a73db59d30b17b3ea31492e0981f"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-wopo-note",
        "moduleId": "why-induction",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "note",
        "title": "良序原理为何是支点",
        "markdown": "良序原理保证“若存在反例，则必有一个**最小**反例”，而最小反例可以直接与归纳步骤发生冲突。下面第一归纳法的证明正是沿这条思路展开的。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-well-ordering"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-first-induction",
        "moduleId": "first-induction",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "教材：第一数学归纳法",
        "markdown": "**定理（数学归纳法）**：设 $P(n)$ 是关于正整数的命题。假设以下两条成立：\n\n- I1：$P(1)$ 成立；\n- I2：若 $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$ 且 $P(k)$ 成立，则 $P(k+1)$ 成立。\n\n那么对任意正整数 $n$，$P(n)$ 都成立。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000009"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Methods of Proof",
                "Mathematical Induction"
              ],
              "lineStart": 239,
              "lineEnd": 294,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "81684586e40aed2064248f3318f4b7188c78a73db59d30b17b3ea31492e0981f"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-chain-intuition",
        "moduleId": "first-induction",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "链条直觉",
        "markdown": "把 I2 依次代入 $k=1,2,3,\\dots$：由 $P(1)$ 得 $P(2)$，由 $P(2)$ 得 $P(3)$，如此逐项推进，于是每一项都被链条覆盖。因此起点与传播规则缺一不可。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-first-induction"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-base-warning",
        "moduleId": "first-induction",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "warning",
        "title": "起头不可省",
        "markdown": "若缺少 $P(1)$，链条没有起点。I2 只是说“真值一旦落在某项就会继续向后传”，却不能保证它真的落在任何一项上。教材因此特别强调“$P(1)$ 的起头非常重要”。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-first-induction"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-step-is-implication",
        "moduleId": "first-induction",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "misconception",
        "title": "归纳步骤证明的是蕴含",
        "markdown": "**常见误解：第二步要证明 $P(k)$ 为真。** 实际上 I2 要证的是一个蕴含：在**假设** $P(k)$ 成立的条件下推出 $P(k+1)$。你不需要知道 $P(k)$ 究竟是否成立，只需完成这个条件推理；若无法仅由 $P(k)$ 推出 $P(k+1)$，这个方法对当前命题就用不上。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "tb-first-induction"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tb-first-induction-proof",
        "moduleId": "first-induction",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "mechanism",
        "title": "教材：用最小反例证明定理",
        "markdown": "**证明思路（反证法 + 良序原理）**：假设并非所有正整数都使 $P(n)$ 成立，则使 $P(n)$ 不成立的正整数构成非空集合，由良序原理存在最小元 $m$。因 $P(1)$ 成立，故 $m \\neq 1$，从而 $m-1$ 是正整数且 $m-1<m$。由 $m$ 的最小性知 $P(m-1)$ 成立；再由 I2 得 $P(m)$ 成立，与 $P(m)$ 不成立矛盾。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-d79ad0eadaa0dc69704ecc53",
